From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:09:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, sechost, advapi32: Keep the event tracing sessions of
 a process, as Windows 11 does.

StartTrace starts a session of the process: a private in-process logger as Office starts one for its own log, a
log file, buffers in memory or a real-time session, checked in the order Windows checks.  EnableTraceEx2 tells the
providers registered in the process -- at once for a private session, from a thread of its own for another, waiting
when asked to -- what all the sessions that enable them want together, classic providers with the logger handle
Windows packs; what they write goes into the log file in the format Windows writes, which tracerpt reads, or to
consumers in the process.  OpenTrace and ProcessTrace read real-time sessions and log files, as EVENT_RECORDs or
EVENT_TRACEs; TraceEvent, TraceMessage and the activity ID calls work.  Event logs and event sources get real handles,
with the server and source checks Windows makes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

